His parents were in Branson.

259
00:13:37,401 --> 00:13:40,237
That's incredible. I totally believed you.

260
00:13:41,071 --> 00:13:42,071
Details.

261
00:13:42,114 --> 00:13:44,533
Now get out of here, I got to finish reading this.

262
00:13:45,993 --> 00:13:48,704
Thank you, Georgie, that was very helpful.

263
00:13:50,247 --> 00:13:51,498
Did you hear that?

264
00:13:51,790 --> 00:13:52,499
What?

265
00:13:52,708 --> 00:13:55,043
Sounds like Georgie and Sheldon are getting along.

266
00:13:55,252 --> 00:13:56,252
Really?

267
00:13:56,837 --> 00:13:57,837
That can't be right.

268
00:13:58,005 --> 00:13:59,006
I just heard it.

269
00:13:59,172 --> 00:14:01,133
Maybe there's hope for those two after all.

270
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:03,510
Or it's a sign of the apocalypse.

271
00:14:03,719 --> 00:14:05,387
Honey, I'm-I'm watching this.

272
00:14:10,892 --> 00:14:14,354
So you'll have to find someone else to hold your ankles in pe. Today.

273
00:14:14,563 --> 00:14:15,856
I'm sorry, what?

274
00:14:16,064 --> 00:14:18,859
I've suffered a terrible injury and won't be able to attend.

275
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:20,067
What happened?

276
00:14:20,402 --> 00:14:21,486
See for yourself.

277
00:14:24,114 --> 00:14:28,617
"Dear coach Wilkins, please excuse my son, Sheldon, "from p.E.

278
00:14:28,994 --> 00:14:33,874
"He has experienced a testicular hernia, "and needs to rest for the next six to eight weeks.

279
00:14:34,082 --> 00:14:35,709
Sincerely, Mary Cooper."

280
00:14:37,878 --> 00:14:39,046
Testicular hernia?

281
00:14:39,254 --> 00:14:41,590
That's called details.

282
00:14:43,383 --> 00:14:45,177
Ooh, that's rough.

283
00:14:45,594 --> 00:14:46,219
Hmm.

284
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:47,137
How'd it happen?

285
00:14:47,346 --> 00:14:54,686
It's hard to say, but some risk factors include: Heavy lifting, a chronic cough and repetitive straining during bowel movements.

286
00:14:55,312 --> 00:14:56,396
I've been there.

287
00:14:56,605 --> 00:14:58,190
Hmm. All right.

288
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:01,568
Guess I'll see you in... Six to eight weeks.

289
00:15:08,241 --> 00:15:14,831
I don't know if other supervillains started their careers by getting out of re, but that's where I began.

290
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:20,504
Emboldened by my faux hernia, I started taking books out of the library...

291
00:15:21,296 --> 00:15:23,423
Without getting the cards stamped.

292
00:15:23,632 --> 00:15:24,901
You didn't check out those books.

293
00:15:24,925 --> 00:15:25,926
I know.

294
00:15:26,843 --> 00:15:30,680
Before you judge me too harshly, I always brought them back on time.

295
00:15:30,931 --> 00:15:33,558
I was a rule-breaker, not a lunatic.

296
00:15:33,975 --> 00:15:41,566
But perhaps my most satisfying transgression was duping my sister into relinquishing control of the TV.

297
00:15:43,652 --> 00:15:44,652
Hello.

298
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:46,279
What's that for?

299
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:50,117
Oh, this? I was just digging for money in meemaw's backyard.

300
00:15:50,534 --> 00:15:51,952
There's money there?

301
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,454
Oh, yes. I already found 75 cents.

302
00:15:54,996 --> 00:15:56,289
Who do you think left it?

303
00:15:57,499 --> 00:16:00,210
If I were to guess, I'd say pirates with holes in their pockets.

304
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:02,546
Can I use your shovel?

305
00:16:03,422 --> 00:16:04,965
Be my guest.

306
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:07,509
Oh, baby, I'm gonna be rich.

307
00:16:10,387 --> 00:16:13,640
Today, we're going to learn about sir Isaac Newton.

308
00:16:14,433 --> 00:16:15,433
Hello, old friend.

309
00:16:15,517 --> 00:16:17,161
One of the world's greatest scientists...

310
00:16:21,773 --> 00:16:22,773
See you tomorrow, Wayne.

311
00:16:22,858 --> 00:16:24,401
You have a good one, George.

312
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:26,445
Hey, how's your son doing?

313
00:16:26,695 --> 00:16:27,695
Georgie?

314
00:16:27,863 --> 00:16:29,156
No, the smart one.

315
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:32,033
He's fine. Why?

316
00:16:32,242 --> 00:16:33,910
What about the hernia?

317
00:16:34,286 --> 00:16:35,286
What hernia?

318
00:16:35,454 --> 00:16:37,330
The one your wife said he had.

319
00:16:41,168 --> 00:16:42,752
Happened to me while I was in the army.

320
00:16:42,961 --> 00:16:46,173
I was in a bar in Georgia, tried to lift up this big gal.

321
00:16:47,215 --> 00:16:49,050
Swear I could hear something pop down there.

322
00:16:49,259 --> 00:16:50,594
Sheldon gave you this note?

323
00:16:50,802 --> 00:16:51,802
Yeah.

324
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:53,263
I didn't write this.

325
00:16:53,472 --> 00:16:54,472
You sure?

326
00:16:54,806 --> 00:16:55,825
Looks like your handwriting.

327
00:16:55,849 --> 00:16:57,452
It's got that little swoopy thing going on.

328
00:16:57,476 --> 00:16:58,476
I didn't write it.

329
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:01,104
And I think I'd know if my son had a hernia.

330
00:17:01,313 --> 00:17:04,232
So what, Sheldon forged a letter to get out of re?

331
00:17:04,483 --> 00:17:05,692
Looks like it.

332
00:17:06,443 --> 00:17:07,443
How about that.

333
00:17:08,361 --> 00:17:09,988
Don't be proud of him.

334
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,908
Can't help it. First time he ever seemed like my kid.

335
00:17:14,242 --> 00:17:16,578
Do you have any idea what's gotten into him?

336
00:17:18,455 --> 00:17:19,455
I might.

337
00:17:19,706 --> 00:17:20,790
Well?

338
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:23,126
Have you ever heard of...

339
00:17:24,127 --> 00:17:26,880
Mobokachi kaboom?

340
00:17:27,339 --> 00:17:28,048
Wait.

341
00:17:28,298 --> 00:17:30,675
Koshimaki Magoo.

342
00:17:31,134 --> 00:17:32,928
Wait a minute, I'm gonna get this.

343
00:17:36,681 --> 00:17:42,521
"Dear professor proton, "I would very much like to meet you, "and I only have three weeks to live.

344
00:17:42,729 --> 00:17:45,232
"Please come visit me here in medford, Texas.

345
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,900
"Sincerely, Sheldon Cooper.

346
00:17:47,108 --> 00:17:49,152
P.s. My meemaw makes excellent brisket."

347
00:17:49,361 --> 00:17:50,028
Sheldon.

348
00:17:50,237 --> 00:17:51,821
Would you like to explain this note?

349
00:17:54,241 --> 00:17:55,242
Well?

350
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:57,451
I was trying to be more like Georgie.

351
00:17:57,619 --> 00:17:58,912
That's a dumb idea.

352
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,748
We don't want Georgie to be like Georgie.

353
00:18:02,415 --> 00:18:05,460
Well, let me start by saying how very sorry I am.

354
00:18:12,092 --> 00:18:20,350
Despite my explanation that I was embracing my inner kirk, my mother had me make amends for all my misdeeds.

355
00:18:20,642 --> 00:18:25,146
Starting in the library, where I had to reshelve hundreds of books.

356
00:18:25,564 --> 00:18:27,899
Well, to be honest, that one was a hoot.

357
00:18:28,441 --> 00:18:32,571
The amends got worse when coach Wilkins made me climb the rope.

358
00:18:33,154 --> 00:18:38,326
Lacking any upper body strength, I hung there like a salami in a deli window.

359
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:46,543
And finally, I had to apologize to my meemaw, who was an unfortunate victim of my sister's treasure hunt.
